  "Number": 2,
  "Question": "A small bottle of shampoo can hold \\(35\\) milliliters of shampoo, whereas a large bottle can hold \\(500\\) milliliters of shampoo. Jasmine wants to buy the minimum number of small bottles necessary to completely fill a large bottle. How many bottles must she buy?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(11\\)",
    "B": "\\(12\\)",
    "C": "\\(13\\)",
    "D": "\\(14\\)",
    "E": "\\(15\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "E",
  "Solution": "Divide the required amount by the amount in one small bottle:\n\\[\n500=14\\times35+10.\n\\]\nThus \\(14\\) full small bottles provide \\(490\\) milliliters, leaving \\(10\\) milliliters still needed. Any smaller number provides even less, so at least \\(15\\) bottles are necessary.\n\nA fifteenth bottle contains enough to supply those last \\(10\\) milliliters; Jasmine can leave the rest in that bottle. Therefore the minimum is \\(\\boxed{15}\\) bottles, choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{E}}\\).",
